\p{How can algebra and geometry organize induction and background
variation? [Gaussian elimination](fdip-000F) gives a finite example;
the [synthesis conjecture](fdip-003X) and
[finite interfaces](fdip-003Y) distinguish this result from the
further maps required.}

\p{The diagram gives the intended route through the explorations
and this synthesis. The compatibility tests and larger proposals are
planned, as is [what the structure fixes and leaves free](fdip-009G).
The existing conjecture and finite interfaces below remain distinct from
those future investigations.}

\transclude{fdip-009H}
